==Tips & Tricks==
* If combined with Shark V4, Venom is very good in teaming situations as the constant tick damage will refill Shark's Leviathan's Armor, providing more survivability.
* Venom's transformation with Ghoul V4 is very potent against Rumbling Waters], as the user can spam all their moves and get their V4 in a matter of seconds, making this combination just as good as Magma].
* It is recommended to wait out moves before using them, since the poison tick cannot stack, and will render most moves null.
** An example of this is avoiding using '''[X]''' after using '''[F]'''. This is because the ticks from '''[F]''' deal very high damage, but get cancelled by '''[X]'''. During the tick duration, the player can stun the enemy, or even use the '''[Z]''' move, as it does not reset poison. 
** This also applies for the '''[C]''' move, which, contrary to popular belief, is only useful for self defense. It gets reset by '''[X]''' during combos, making the move pointless.
*** Due to these conditions, Venom may be rather hard to use in active combat efficiently, however, the Strong Grip Enchantment can help with this, as it provides valuable damage to supporting Sword and Guns.

