==Trivia==
* Venom is one of three [[natural]] fruits that has a transformation and is not considered as a [[beast]]. The other two fruits are [[Rubber]] and [[Magnet]].
* [[Transformation]] model was made by Mary (@Marubravery on X).
* Venom is the only fruit that starts with the letter "V".
* Venom shares similarities with [[Magma]], as both have abilities that create puddles that cause damage over time. Their damage stacks as well (However with some exceptions), making them deal incredible amounts of damage.
* The transformation works similarly to the Awakened Buddha, gaining reduced dash and acceleration buffs from accessories.
* Sometimes, transformed {{Ability|C}} only does one cycle of poison damage. This is a very old, unpatched bug.
* Despite Venom having a [[transformation]] and having a [[Power Meter|Meter]] mechanic, it is not a [[Beast]] fruit, making it the first [[Natural]] fruit with a transformation and a meter mechanic, with [[Magnet]] being the second.
** Likewise, it does not turn the player ''into'' venom, it just uses venom in the form of attacks, along with the ability to encase oneself in it.
*** it is not based off of an animal, rather, a natural substance, hence why Venom is not a [[Beast]] or [[Elemental]] [[Blox Fruits|fruit]].
* Just like [[Dragon]] and [[T-Rex]], Venom's [[Fury Meter]] needs 1 minute and 30 seconds to fully recharge.
* Venom is the first [[Natural]] fruit to have a [[Power Meter|power meter]], the second being [[Shadow]] and the third being [[Spirit]].
* Venom, along with [[Spirit|Spirit,]] are the only fruits to retain their original physical fruit models since [[Updates/20|Update 20]].
* Venom, [[Love]] and [[T-Rex]] are the only fruits to have a skill whose name has an apostrophe in it. One might think [[Control]]'s {{Ability|Control|X|2}}'''Slice N’ Dice''' also has one too, but it's actually a quotation mark instead of an apostrophe.
* Venom and [[Shadow]] are the only {{Mythical}} fruits without M1s.
* Venom is the only fruit with a [[transformation]] and no M1s.
* Venom is of the three fruits that share a damaging leap passive. The other ones being Buddha] and [[Mammoth]].
* {{Ability|F}} duration isn't infinite, so it cannot deal infinite damage to NPCs or guarantee getting the user from island to island.
* When transformed, Venom's skills turn pink-ish instead of turning into the usual purple.
** Under extremely bright lighting, the Transformation's model gains a striking pink.
* Venom, [[Spirit]] and [[Dragon (Classic)|Classic Dragon]] are the only fruits not to receive a model rework in [[Updates/20|Update 20]].
* As of the 2026 Halloween Update, Venom is unavailable to be purchased through the Blox Fruit Dealer, and is 'in progress'.

